          %h2#references References
          %p
            Definition in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+complete+Segal+spaces"} n-fold complete Segal spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+n-categories"} Segal n-categories
            are due to the (unpublished) thesis
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                \-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
                as a closed model category
              PhD (2005)
          %p
            The definition in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+spaces"} Theta spaces
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Rezk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              %em A cartesian presentation of weak n-categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0901.3602"}> arXiv:0901.3602
              )
          %p
            An iterartive definition in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+complete+Segal+spaces"} n-fold complete Segal spaces
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,2)
                \-Categories and the Goodwillie Calculus I
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.0462"}> arXiv:0905.0462
              )
          %p A summary of definitions and some known comparison results can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julie+Bergner"}> Julie Bergner
              ,
              %em
                Models for
                = succeed "-Categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
              , in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
              %p
                AMS (2011) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.0110"}> arXiv:1011.0110
                )
          %p
            A textbook account focusing on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+complete+Segal+spaces"} n-fold complete Segal spaces
            and related models is in
          %ul
            %li#Paoli19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simona+Paoli"}> Simona Paoli
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Simplicial Methods for Higher Categories – Segal-type Models of Weak
                  = succeed "-Categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-05674-2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-05674-2
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/bfm%3A978-3-030-05674-2%2F1.pdf"} toc pdf
          %p One axiomatic characterization is in
          %ul
            %li#BarwickSchommerPries
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"} Chris Schommer-Pries
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Unicity of the Homotopy Theory of Higher Categories
              %strong 34
              (2021) 1011-1058 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1112.0040"}> arXiv:1112.0040
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://prezi.com/w0ykkhh5mxak/the-uniqueness-of-the-homotopy-theory-of-higher-categories/"} slides
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/972"} doi:10.1090/jams/972
          %p
            Comparison of models (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Θ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta_{n+1}
            \-spaces and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} enriched (infinity,1)-categories
            in
            = succeed "-spaces)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
